  "hypothesis": "Condition the aggressive first stake on the measured amount of positively correlated long inventory to retain extra return while reducing stacked risk.",
  "rule": "Pure native Top Coins long first stakes only. Use Pearson correlation of 30 daily log returns ending with the preceding completed UTC daily candle. At the callback, mark each existing filled long quantity at its last closed daily price and add pending entry notional at its placement price. Sum each long notional times max(0, correlation with incoming asset). Native short inventory does not offset the score. Divide by 30% of starting capital plus strictly prior closed campaigns' net PnL (30% multiplies the sum). Boost = 1 + 0.5 * max(0, 1 - overlap / budget). Missing or zero-variance data or nonpositive realized capital means 1x. No leverage, signal, exit or add change.",
  "gate": "Run 2024 first at both costs. Require positive full return above original and return/5m drawdown above fixed 1.25x, full 5m drawdown <= original +1pp, higher return than original in every registered slice, >=60 natural closes, >=20 scoped fills and >=10 boosted scoped fills. If both costs pass, run 65-day temporal comparison with the same economic gates but minimum 20 natural closes, 10 scoped fills and 5 boosted. If it passes, run 20-month historical comparison using the 2024 sample thresholds. Retain all failed runs.",
  "known_history": "The 2024 correlated drawdown incident and all original/flat returns in the three windows were known before designing A14. Historical adaptation, no independent forward evidence. Pure 1.5x no-inventory A08 is separate.",
  "orders_enabled": false
